        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Removes all occurrences of <code class=\"notranslate\">ie: { version_added: false }</code> from the repository, adding them at build time instead.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Partly <span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #25814.\">fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2821338609\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25814\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25814/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25814\">#25814</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26949",
            "title": "enhance(build): add `ie: { version_added: false }` at build time",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-10T09:26:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-30T15:08:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54515?u=b3091d8543234ab43ceedae962b178688740b617&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The current browser implementation of gamut mapping is buggy and not spec compliant. This has accessibility ramifications (the spec ensures that color contrast is preserved, even if a color is beyond what a user can display, but browser don't respect that invariant in their implementation).</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Visit <a href=\"https://vasilis.nl/dingen/bugs/oklch.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://vasilis.nl/dingen/bugs/oklch.html</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The squares should be white and black per spec, they aren't in any browser.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1933631613\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9449\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9449/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9449\">w3c/csswg-drafts#9449</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=255939\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=255939</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1847421\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1847421</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40909194\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40909194</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1340067398\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7610\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7610/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7610\">w3c/csswg-drafts#7610</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1354160102\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7653\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7653/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7653\">w3c/csswg-drafts#7653</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This <span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #26838.\">fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3074538627\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26838\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26838/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26838\">#26838</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26841",
            "title": "Add the lack of proper gamut mapping in OKLch and Oklab. The browser support is thus only parial.",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-01T02:44:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-19T19:39:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pygy",
                "url": "https://github.com/pygy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Safari (Desktop and iOS/iPadOS) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">line-clamp</code> CSS property. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.13.0).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/line-clamp\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/line-clamp</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Additional Notes: Looks like Safari dropped support for the unprefixed version since no other browser supported it.  Confirmed via manual testing.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26771",
            "title": "Update Safari data for line-clamp CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-05-25T00:47:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-10T08:25:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">setTargetAtTime</code> member of the <code class=\"notranslate\">AudioParam</code> API. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.12.13).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/AudioParam/setTargetAtTime\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/AudioParam/setTargetAtTime</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26722",
            "title": "Update Chromium data for api.AudioParam.setTargetAtTime",
            "date_modified": "2025-05-25T00:43:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-06T22:22:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR breaks the \"alternate name\" <code class=\"notranslate\">Feature-Policy</code> into its own feature entries. See <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2860134395\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25950\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25950/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25950\">#25950</a> for further discussion.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are a few issues I have not resolved:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Should we track the individual features/permission names under <code class=\"notranslate\">Feature-Policy</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code>, both, or neither? I've (tentatively) tracked them in both, to preserve the continuity of many of the permissions existing <em>before</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code>.</li>\n<li>Should the <code class=\"notranslate\">Feature-policy</code> features link to any MDN pages (since they're actually for PP)? As a matter of convenience, I did not remove the links from the FP file, but I could do so.</li>\n<li>Should the <code class=\"notranslate\">Feature-policy</code> features link specs? As a matter of convenience, I did not remove the links from the FP file, but I could do so.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2860134395\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25950\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25950/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25950\">#25950</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26708",
            "title": "Unmerge the `Feature-Policy` and `Permissions-Policy` headers",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-01T02:45:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-05T18:46:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR removes the <code class=\"notranslate\">SnapEvent</code> member of the <code class=\"notranslate\">SnapEvent</code> API from BCD. The collector reports that the constructor is an illegal constructor in Chromium.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/SnapEvent/SnapEvent\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/SnapEvent/SnapEvent</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26687",
            "title": "Remove api.SnapEvent.SnapEvent from BCD",
            "date_modified": "2025-05-25T00:47:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-01T14:08:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Firefox and Firefox Android for the <code class=\"notranslate\">load_event</code> member of the <code class=\"notranslate\">SVGElement</code> API. The <code class=\"notranslate\">alternative_name</code> property was incorrectly used in this context.</p>",
